   "notes": "Medium = standard M9 minimal salts + 10 mL/L Wolfe's minerals (ATCC MD-TMS, 1:100 dilution) + 4.5 mg/L thiamine (B1); carbon = 20 mmol/L glucose (10 mmol/L in 13C-tracer runs); aerobic. The trace-metal block (Mo, Se, W, Ni, B, Al, EDTA) was hidden inside the MD-TMS stock and was absent before; it is expanded here from the ATCC catalog formulation, so trace concentrations are catalog-derived not paper-stated (hence medium confidence). Wolfe's vitamins (MD-VS) were also purchased but were NOT added to the aerobic growth medium (only Wolfe's minerals + B1 were), so the vitamin mix is deliberately"
